## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)

- hi-a #2 treats the R3 softening (“some judgments … not a guaranteed result”) as a mistranslation of “courts currently generally impose”. The English source does say “generally”, but this campaign already required that sentence to stay softened. Restoring सामान्यतः would make the result sentence positive.
- hi-a #24 and hi-b #32 are right about Indian lakh grouping and wrong for this checker. ACCEPTED-ROUND says not to use lakh/crore grouping. Western commas stay.
- hi-b #19 is not a translation defect. The reviewer notes that the English source skips from 5 to 7 as well. Renumbering Hindi would leave the Korean and English outlines.
- hi-b #18 is right that U+200B is noise, and wrong as an edit: the checker requires the Korean source’s ZWSP count.
- hi-b #27 is right that 013/015 are still one sentence per paragraph, and wrong as an edit: merging those blocks changes the block count.
- hi-a #10 correctly reports that the German pricing sentence says sending an inquiry on this page is free of charge. Adding that Hindi sentence would state a free service. The product rule does not allow that sentence to be made positive. The ban on a free first meeting was left as it is.
